    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="2.11">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IVAtr">IV Atr</ref> 2.11</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="2.11" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="234" ed="#liebermann"/>De dosseris cum gallinis I gallina telon., et de<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IVAtr_2-11.lnote.oe.12"/> uno dossero cum ouis V oua telonei, si ueniant<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IVAtr_2-11.lnote.oe.13"/> ad mercatum.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="la" source="#robertson" n="2.11" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="72" ed="#robertson"/>De dosseris cum gallinis I gallina telonei, et de<ptr type="editorNote" n="13" target="#IVAtr_2-11.robnote.fn.13"/> uno dossero cum ovis V ova telonei, si veniant ad mercatum.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IVAtr_2-11.lnote.de.1"/><pb n="235" ed="#liebermann"/>Von Tragekörben<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IVAtr_2-11.lnote.de.2"/> mit Hühnern: je 1 Huhn Zoll, und von je einem Tragekorb mit Eiern 5 Eier Zoll, wenn sie zu Markte kommen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">From panniers with hens: 1 hen as toll each, and from each pannier with eggs 5 eggs as toll, if they come to market.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="73" ed="#robertson"/>From hampers<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#IVAtr_2-11.robnote.n.1"/> with hens, one hen [is given] as toll, and from one hamper of eggs, five eggs as toll, if they come to the market.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IVAtr_2-11.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">234</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt MHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in MHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IVAtr_2-11.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">234</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ueniat <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ueniat Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IVAtr_2-11.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">164</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Auch das Folgende bezieht Höhlbaum auf Deutsche: mit Unrecht laut 2, 12</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Höhlbaum refers what follows to the Germans as well: wrongly, according to 2, 12</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IVAtr_2-11.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">164</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Rückenkorb’ Ducange nur hierher. Schon im Londoner Französisch und Latein 14. Jhs. ist <hi rend="italic">dosser</hi> ein Packkorb, auch vom Pferd oder Boot getragen, u. a. für Fische, <hi rend="italic">Mun. Gildhal</hi>. I 235. 343. 375; so mittel- und neuengl.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘Back-basket’: Ducange, for this passage only. Already in the London French and Latin of the 14th cent. <hi rend="italic">dosser</hi> is a pack-basket, also one carried by a horse or a boat, used among other things for fish, <hi rend="italic">Mun. Gildhal</hi>. I 235. 343. 375; so too in Middle and Modern English</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="IVAtr_2-11.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">324</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">i.e.</hi> hampers carried on the back.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IVAtr_2-11.robnote.fn.13" n="13" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope></bibl><label>de</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Om. M, Hk.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
